摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Memory library for building stateful agents","id":"gh:689777286","install_available":false,"language":"Python","name":"honcho","slug":"plastic-labs/honcho","topics":["agent-memory","agentic-rag","ai","ai-agents","ai-memory","context-engineering","continual-learning","dsh-plugin","llm","memory"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Memory library for building stateful agents"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"**Honcho is memory infrastructure for building stateful agents that understand changing people, agen"},{"id":"p2s2","text":"ts, groups, projects, and ideas over time.**"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Store messages and events, let Honcho reason in the background, then query peer representations, ses"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"sion context, search results, or natural-language insights from any model or framework. Use it manag"},{"id":"p3s3","text":"ed at api.honcho.dev, run a local stack with `honcho start`, or self-host the FastAPI server yoursel"},{"id":"p3s4","text":" at api.honcho.dev, run a local stack with `honcho start`, or self-host the FastAPI server yourself."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Using Honcho as your memory system will earn your agents higher retention, more trust, and help you "},{"id":"p4s2","text":"build data moats to out-compete incumbents."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"> Honcho has defined the Pareto Frontier of Agent Memory. Watch the video, check out our evals page,"},{"id":"p5s2","text":" and read the blog post for more detail."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Contents"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- Start Here\n- Why Honcho\n- The Honcho Loop\n- Quickstart\n- What Honcho Gives You\n- Integrations\n- CL"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"I\n- Core Concepts\n- Benchmarks & Evals\n- Self-hosting\n- Configuration\n- Architecture\n- SDKs\n- Learn "},{"id":"p7s3","text":"More\n- Contributing\n- License"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"The Honcho project is split between several repositories, with this one hosting the core service log"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"ic — implemented as a FastAPI server. Client SDKs for Python and TypeScript live in the `sdks/` dire"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"ctory. The `honcho-cli` package lives here too."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Start Here"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| I want to...                           | Path                                                     "},{"id":"p10s2","text":"  | Get started                   |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| Give my coding agent persistent memory | Claude Code, Cursor, Grok Bot, OpenCode, Kilo Code, OpenC"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"law, Hermes, or any MCP client | Integrations |\n| Add memory to my product               | Python or"},{"id":"p11s3","text":" TypeScript SDK                                   | Quickstart     |\n| Run Honcho locally           "},{"id":"p11s4","text":"          | Install CLI, then `honcho start --setup`                   | CLI                   |\n| I"},{"id":"p11s5","text":"nspect a deployment                   | `honcho workspace inspect`, `honcho doctor`                |"},{"id":"p11s6","text":" CLI                   |\n| Self-host from source                  | Docker Compose or local developm"},{"id":"p11s7","text":"ent                        | Self-hosting |"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Why Honcho"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"| Capability              | What it means                                                           "},{"id":"p13s2","text":"            | What it means                                                                        |"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"| Reasoning-first memory  | Extracts conclusions from conversations and events, not just matching ch"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"unks.        |\n| Peer-centric model      | Tracks users, agents, groups, projects, and ideas as enti"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"ties that change over time. |\n| Multi-peer perspective  | Models what one peer knows about another w"},{"id":"p14s4","text":"hen configured.                            |\n| Managed or self-hosted  | Use `api.honcho.dev`, `honc"},{"id":"p14s5","text":"ho start` locally, or run the FastAPI server yourself.    |\n| Agent-tool integrations | MCP, Claude "},{"id":"p14s6","text":"Code, Cursor, Grok Bot, OpenCode, Kilo Code, OpenClaw, Hermes.  |"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## The Honcho Loop"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"1. **Store** conversations, events, documents, or tool traces as messages on a session.\n2. **Reason*"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"* — Honcho processes the queue in the background and updates peer representations.\n3. **Query** — as"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"k Honcho for context, search results, peer representations, or a natural-language answer.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## What Honcho Gives You"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"| Need                               | API                                                          "},{"id":"p18s2","text":"ed                               | API                                                             |"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"| Save interaction history           | `session.add_messages(...)`                                  "},{"id":"p19s2","text":"   |\n| Ask what Honcho knows about a peer | `peer.chat(...)`                                        "},{"id":"p19s3","text":"        |\n| Ask across the whole workspace     | `honcho.chat(...)` / `honcho.chat_stream(...)`     "},{"id":"p19s4","text":"             |\n| Get prompt-ready context           | `session.context(...).to_openai(...)` / `.to_a"},{"id":"p19s5","text":"nthropic(...)`    |\n| Hybrid search (BM25 + vector)      | `peer.search(...)`, `session.search(...)`"},{"id":"p19s6","text":", `honcho.search(...)` |\n| Low-latency static representations | `peer.representation(...)`, `session"},{"id":"p19s7","text":".representation(...)`       |\n| Import documents                   | `session.upload_file(...)`     "},{"id":"p19s8","text":"                                 |\n| Inspect background processing      | `honcho.queue_status(...)`"},{"id":"p19s9","text":"                                      |"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"See the full SDK Reference and API Reference."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## Architecture"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Honcho splits into two services: **Storage** (workspaces, peers, sessions, scopes, messages, interna"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"l collections) and **Insights** (reasoning, conclusions, representations, summaries, the chat endpoi"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"nt). Storage is synchronous via the API; Insights is asynchronous via a background queue consumed by"},{"id":"p22s4","text":" the deriver worker process."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"**Key features:**"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"- **Rich Reasoning System** — multiple implementation methods that extract conclusions from interact"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"ions and build comprehensive representations of peers\n- **Chat Endpoint** — reasoning-informed respo"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"nses that integrate conclusions with current context\n- **Background Processing** — asynchronous proc"},{"id":"p24s4","text":"essing pipeline for expensive operations like representation updates and session summarization\n- **M"},{"id":"p24s5","text":"ulti-Provider Support** — configurable LLM providers for different use cases"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Storage primitives in detail"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"Honcho contains several different primitives used for storing application and\npeer data. This data i"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"s used for managing conversations, modeling peer\nidentity, building RAG applications, and more."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"The philosophy behind Honcho is to provide a platform that is peer-centric and\neasily scalable from "},{"id":"p27s2","text":"a single user to a million."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"Below is a mapping of the different primitives and their relationships."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"**Relationship Details:**"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"- A **Workspace** contains multiple **Peers** and **Scopes**.\n- **Peers** and **Sessions** have a ma"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"ny-to-many relationship (peers can participate in multiple sessions, sessions can have multiple peer"},{"id":"p31s3","text":"s).\n- **Scopes** and **Sessions** have a many-to-many relationship (a session can belong to several "},{"id":"p31s4","text":"scopes; a scope groups many sessions).\n- **Messages** belong to a session and are labelled by their "},{"id":"p31s5","text":"source peer.\n- **Internal collections** of vector-embedded **documents** are keyed by `(observer, ob"},{"id":"p31s6","text":"served)` peer pairs. They are not directly exposed via the API; the observations stored in them are "},{"id":"p31s7","text":"exposed as **Conclusions**."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"Users familiar with APIs such as the OpenAI Assistants API will be familiar with\nmuch of the mapping"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"familiar with APIs such as the OpenAI Assistants API will be familiar with\nmuch of the mapping here."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
